Message-ID: <2CB2DA8E426F3541AB1907F98ABA657075F4BF33@icexch-m1.ic.ac.uk>


Hi again, 

it is not so much a technical limitation than a theoretical one. There is no reason why sPCA should give structures which match perfectly geographic clusters. Moreover, if you used a different color scheme (i.e., other than translation onto RGB scale)  for your groups, then colors won't match (even if the sPCA structures matched your clusters remarkably).

Cheers
Thibaut


